Also, note the document-level dispatch checks `q["from"]` presence (even empty value `?from=`). With `?from=` (empty), q["from"] exists → isExport → parse: raw == "" → treated as default 0. Consistent with document-level. Good — mirror exactly.

Also empty `?to=` → default no upper bound. Consistent.

Now README: add documentation for the session-level export. The README section for session changes is at line 92-98. I should extend it or add a new section. The task says "导出与分页共用 README 已公开的会话变更读取路径". I'll add a section after the session changes section describing the export, mirroring the document-level export doc.

Now tests: create `session_changes_export_test.go` in internal/server. Let me look at existing test helpers and changes_export_test.go for patterns.

